  "body": "## Summary\nFix high severity security issue in `frontend-react/src/utils/apiClient.js`.\n\n## Vulnerability\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **ID** | V-001 |\n| **Severity** | HIGH |\n| **Scanner** | multi_agent_ai |\n| **Rule** | `V-001` |\n| **File** | `frontend-react/src/utils/apiClient.js:12` |\n| **Assessment** | Likely exploitable |\n\n**Description**: The frontend API client uses a configurable API_BASE_URL without enforcing HTTPS protocol. While the backend has HTTPS detection logic in security_headers.go, the frontend does not validate or enforce that connections are made exclusively over HTTPS, allowing potential downgrade attacks or MITM interception.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Exploitation scenario**: An attacker in a man-in-the-middle position could intercept HTTP requests, downgrade HTTPS connections, or intercept unencrypted traffic to steal session tokens, credentials, or manipulate API.\n\n**Scanner confirmation**: multi_agent_ai rule `V-001` flagged this pattern.\n\n**Production code**: This file is in the production codebase, not test-only code.\n\n## Threat Model Context\n\nThis is a containerized service - vulnerabilities may be exploitable depending on network exposure.\n\n## Changes\n- `frontend-react/src/utils/apiClient.js`\n\n## Behavior Preservation\nThe change is scoped to 1 file on the vulnerable path.\n\n---\n*Automated security fix by [OrbisAI Security](https://orbisappsec.com)*\n\n<!-- orbis-meta: rule=V-001 scanner=multi_agent_ai -->\n",
